auth {
  mode: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

docs {
  # Kitaably API

  Every request inherits a bearer token from this collection. `00-auth` fills it in —
  run that first, or run the whole collection top to bottom.

  The folders are numbered because they build on each other: books before assessments,
  assessments before attempts. `bru run --env local -r` walks the whole product in one
  pass: upload a book, share it, ask the tutor, generate a paper, publish it, sit it,
  mark it, release it.

  `07-boundaries` is the interesting folder. Every request in it is *expected to fail* —
  they assert 404, because that is what this API returns when you reach for something
  that is not yours. Not 403: a 403 on somebody else's row confirms the row exists.
}
